But note that method is void, no return value. Use edge variable (parameter). So assert: (edge == null) => this.peekEdge() == null && (edge != null) => this.peekEdge() == edge.

But need parentheses to ensure grouping: (edge == null => this.peekEdge() == null) && (edge != null => this.peekEdge() == edge). However syntax: A => B is binary, lower priority than &&, but we should parenthesize each implication.

Thus final assert:

assert (edge == null => this.peekEdge() == null) && (edge != null => this.peekEdge() == edge);

